# repositories/cloned/.gitkeep
# =============================================================================
# PURPOSE: Preserve this directory in Git version control
# =============================================================================
#
# This directory will store cloned copies of scanned GitHub repositories.
#
# ISOLATION MODEL — Each repository scan is fully isolated:
#
#   repositories/cloned/
#   ├── SCAN-550e8400/          ← One folder per scan (named by Scan ID)
#   │   ├── main.tf             ← Cloned repo files preserved as-is
#   │   ├── variables.tf
#   │   └── modules/
#   │       └── network/
#   │           └── main.tf
#   ├── SCAN-a1b2c3d4/          ← Separate scan of a different repo (or same repo)
#   │   └── terraform/
#   │       └── aws/
#   │           └── main.tf
#   └── SCAN-ff001122/
#       └── ...
#
# KEY DESIGN PROPERTIES:
#
#   - Multiple repositories can be scanned simultaneously (different Scan IDs)
#   - The same repository can be scanned multiple times (each scan gets a new Scan ID)
#   - Scan history is preserved by retaining each cloned directory
#   - Evidence is isolated per Scan ID — no cross-contamination between scans
#   - The original repository structure is preserved unchanged inside each scan folder
#     (the framework adapts to the repo, not vice versa)
#
# CLONING BEHAVIOUR (future — scripts/clone_repository.py):
#   - `git clone <repository_url> repositories/cloned/<scan_id>/`
#   - Specific branch can be targeted (defaults to main/master)
#   - Shallow clone supported for large repositories
#   - Clone timestamp and commit SHA recorded in scan metadata
#
# IMPORTANT:
#   - The contents of repositories/cloned/ are NOT committed to this repository
#   - Each scan directory is excluded via .gitignore (repositories/cloned/*)
#   - Only this .gitkeep file is tracked by Git
# =============================================================================
